WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.433
This curve shows loss as the weight changes. Start at zero,
with loss nine. The minimum is at three.

2
00:00:06.433 --> 00:00:13.967
The gradient is twice the difference between the weight and
three. At zero it is minus six. The curve slopes down to the
right.

3
00:00:13.967 --> 00:00:21.833
We subtract the gradient times a learning rate. With a
negative gradient, should the weight move left or right? Pause
here.

4
00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:29.767
Use learning rate zero point two. Subtracting a negative moves
right to one point two. Loss falls to three point two four.

5
00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:35.900
Recompute the slope at the new weight: minus three point six.
The next weight is one point nine two.

6
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:42.200
A third update reaches two point three five two. The steps
shrink as the weight approaches the minimum.

7
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:50.700
Step size matters. A learning rate of one point two jumps past
the minimum and increases the loss to seventeen point six
four.

